 "text": "Hi, how have you been? I usually use the mornings for them, so they don't interrupt active days. Pick morning time zone that works for both of you. Then save weekday dates in the evening, so they' easy to reschedule if weather turns bad. Both are good. Some people mix them up and get confused, so one each gives a clear signal. Email it and she'll appreciate it. You can also ask at the front of each class if there are any date evenings. Teachers usually know. Handwriting makes it feel special. Print each one and fold each one on full sheet of paper so they look like little secrets. Stick them in nice journal or calendar so they' easy to find.",
